  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Legislation wind energy development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the assessment of existing normative framework and the development of comprehensive legal and regulatory changes required to unlock the potential of large-scale wind energy development in Ukraine. Desired changes will cover environmental, construction, land, grid connection and regulatory aspects in accordance with EU-accepted overriding public interest approach. The results of this project will be shared with the Ministry of Energy of Ukraine and the Office of the President of Ukraine, and will be used to foster the increase of low carbon energy sources based on wind energy in the country. It is expected that these changes in the regulatory framework related to development procedures and facilitating investment in the short term, until 2030, could result in additional +10 GW wind projects and help create a portfolio of projects for implementation in the 2030s with a total capacity larger than 20 GW wind development in the country. The project contributes to the National Economy Strategy of Ukraine until 2030. This strategy targets a 25% renewable energy sources and renewable energy storage (RES) share in electricity supply by 2030, in line with the RED II EU Directive.</narrative>
  </description>
